Diagnosis found a container PID-namespace mismatch: Lean calls `readlink("/proc/<getpid>/exe")`, but this audit container exposes the executable only through `/proc/self/exe`; the exact failing path was captured. I’m applying a narrow runtime compatibility shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that substitutes only that self-executable lookup. It does not modify any candidate, provenance input, trusted checker, or Lean source, and I’ll record the shim source/hash with the successful rerun.
